flowchart TD
    accTitle: BlaBla concept
    accDescr: Owner intent is written into a BlaBla project as two different things. Authored project memory holds Mission, System, Process and Knowledge, which coding agents query through blabla status and explain but which never decide completion. Executable contracts hold Structure and Behavior, which blabla finish verifies to decide OVERALL GREEN. A bounded task holds transient scope, deliverables and findings for one change, and blabla challenge checks the recorded account of the work against that evidence without deciding completion. Agents write ordinary implementation code; BlaBla does not launch them.
    intent["Owner intent<br/>purpose, architecture, constraints"]
    subgraph authored["Authored project memory — queried, never gating"]
        memory["Mission · System<br/>Process · Knowledge"]
    end
    subgraph executable["Executable contracts — verified, decide completion"]
        contracts["Structure<br/>Behavior"]
    end
    agent["Coding agent<br/>blabla status → explain"]
    implementation["Ordinary implementation<br/>any language"]
    subgraph transient["Transient development state"]
        task[".blabla/tasks<br/>scope · deliverables · findings"]
    end
    challenge["blabla challenge<br/>deterministic check, decides no completion"]
    finish["blabla finish<br/>structure check + behavior campaign"]
    green["OVERALL GREEN<br/>completion allowed"]
    blocked["BLOCKED<br/>RED, YELLOW, STALE or INTERRUPTED"]
    intent --> authored
    intent --> executable
    authored -.informs.-> agent
    agent --> implementation
    agent --> task
    task --> challenge
    challenge -.reconcile.-> agent
    implementation --> finish
    executable --> finish
    finish --> green
    finish --> blocked --> agent
